1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:01,661
The ship is covered with the waves.

2
00:00:02,801 --> 00:00:05,302
And in the stern He is asleep.

3
00:00:06,942 --> 00:00:08,543
The Bible does not say why He sleeps.

4
00:00:09,803 --> 00:00:13,865
They wake Him: Lord, save us: we perish.

5
00:00:15,005 --> 00:00:19,107
He opens His eyes: Why are ye fearful, O ye

6
00:00:19,147 --> 00:00:19,947
of little faith?

7
00:00:20,807 --> 00:00:22,868
Then he arose, and rebuked the winds and the

8
00:00:22,928 --> 00:00:24,669
sea; and there was a great calm.

9
00:00:25,749 --> 00:00:27,950
You'll say easy for Him, He's God.

10
00:00:28,790 --> 00:00:29,310
Exactly.

11
00:00:29,870 --> 00:00:31,451
The One who could sleep through it is the One

12
00:00:31,491 --> 00:00:32,731
who silenced it with a word.

13
00:00:33,932 --> 00:00:35,392
Maybe your own storm is loud right now.

14
00:00:36,353 --> 00:00:39,554
You can pray their short prayer: Lord, save

15
00:00:39,614 --> 00:00:39,914
us.

16
00:00:40,934 --> 00:00:42,315
He doesn't despise little faith.

17
00:00:43,035 --> 00:00:44,796
He grows it by showing you Himself.

18
00:00:45,976 --> 00:00:48,797
Their faith was little, and He still stood

19
00:00:48,837 --> 00:00:49,237
up for them.

20
00:00:50,358 --> 00:00:53,119
He is asking you why are you afraid?
